# teaching_material repository

This repo is the **BAUDOTlab teaching Quarto book** (installation guides, Git,
R packages, LaTeX). It is not the DeCovarT package.

## Layout

- `index.qmd`, chapter folders (`fresh-installation/`, `Git/`, `R/`, `latex/`),
  `_quarto.yml` — book sources; output under `docs/` for GitHub Pages.
- `Config/` — portable dotfiles and **Cursor bundle** (`Config/.cursor/rules/`,
  `Config/.cursor/skills/`). Students copy or symlink into `~/.cursor/`.
- `SNF/` — legacy R Markdown course assets; do not break URLs without intent.

## Conventions

- British English in prose; reproducible Quarto where chunks run.
- Cross-link chapters from `index.qmd`; keep `_quarto.yml` `project.render`
  list in sync when adding chapters.
- LaTeX chapter aligns with `latex/latex-guidelines.qmd` and
  `rules/latex-scientific.mdc`.
- Do not commit secrets, API keys, or machine-specific paths in shared Config.

## Deploying Cursor rules from this bundle

```bash
# user-wide (recommended for teaching defaults)
cp -r Config/.cursor/rules/* ~/.cursor/rules/
cp -r Config/.cursor/skills/* ~/.cursor/skills/

# or per-project
mkdir -p .cursor/rules .cursor/skills
cp -r Config/.cursor/rules/* .cursor/rules/
cp -r Config/.cursor/skills/* .cursor/skills/
```

Install Firecrawl skills separately (see `skills/firecrawl/SKILL.md`).
